     1|/**
     2| * IVX AUTONOMOUS CODER — REAL CODE-WRITING ENGINE.
     3| *
     4| * Owner mandate 2026-07-19: turn IVX IA from a routing system into a REAL
     5| * senior developer that can independently inspect, edit, test, revise, commit,
     6| * and verify real code changes without Rork authoring the patch.
     7| *
     8| * This engine runs a bounded engineering loop:
     9| *
    10| *   INSPECT → PLAN → PATCH → TEST → ANALYZE → REVISE → VERIFY → COMMIT →
    11| *   AWAIT_OWNER_APPROVAL → DEPLOY → PRODUCTION_VERIFY
    12| *
    13| * The LLM (owner-controlled, via ivx-ai-runtime.ts requestIVXAIText) generates
    14| * the patch. The engine applies it, runs real tests + typecheck, and if they
    15| * fail, feeds the error back to the LLM for revision (bounded to
    16| * maximumIterations). When tests pass, the engine commits via the GitHub Git
    17| * Data API (owner-controlled GITHUB_TOKEN). Deploy requires owner approval
    18| * (approvalPolicy: 'owner_gated') and uses render_trigger_deploy.
    19| *
    20| * NOTHING is faked. If the LLM fails to produce a valid patch, the engine
    21| * returns STATUS: BLOCKED with the exact failures. If tests fail after
    22| * maximumIterations, the engine returns STATUS: BLOCKED with the current diff
    23| * and failure output. A job is only marked COMPLETED when a real patch exists,
    24| * relevant tests passed, typecheck passed, and (for code changes) a real commit
    25| * SHA was produced.
    26| */
